result.verified:
- `npx vitest run src/game`: 8 files, 117 tests, all passing.
- `npx tsc --noEmit`: clean for the whole repo.
- Full `npx vitest run`: 38 files, 465 tests, all passing at the time of the run.
- The 500-run property test checks, at every step:
  - lives stay in 0..maxLives and the ladder has 5 rivals;
  - no duplicate Mutations, at most 5;
  - every phase change is an edge in PHASE_EDGES;
  - draft offers are distinct, never owned, always in the profile pool, and pass canOffer;
  - battleSetup is valid in every live phase;
  - a JSON clone taken at a random point mid-run and driven by the same actions stays deep-equal to the original.
- I ran the built thing: a scratchpad script played 3 full runs against the real sim (the sim's crude harness bot on both sides) on every arena, and I read the output. Ladders came out right, e.g. bumble > pip > brood > sable > mora on the first run. Draft offers always included a counter to the next rival. The first-run handicap came out as 0.75 then 0.85, and Crown Level 4 gave bot level 5, the Crown opening at 30 s and an extra rival Mutation.
- Facts read like 'Throne taken at 0:30 | 2 King takedowns | Swarm peak 71' and 'Crown held 3.4 of 10 s | ...'. That run led me to fix 3 things: a '0 rival critters squashed' line, the Throne-survived fact outranking the win reason, and the gullet Thrones being too close (the Throne fell at 0:14).
- On the machine request: I followed design/STUDIO.md. Load average was about 14 on 8 threads and about 2.8 GB RAM was free, so I kept every check in Node (no browser or dev server), ran the full suite only once, and gave the battle-playing tests 60 s timeouts so a busy machine does not fail them.
